// Jatayu — aranya kanda
// Source: Valmiki, Aranya Kanda, sargas 50-51 (verify)
// Migrated from the old script format. Not yet staged for the Ramlila stage.

>> scene sky style=bharni-earth
>> music forest-battle
>> cast jatayu at 0.2 y=-200
Jatayu is asleep on his tree. He is sixty thousand years old. He wakes to a woman calling his name.
JATAYU: Ravana! I am old, and you are young and armed and in a chariot. Still you will not carry her past me. Put her down.
>> play jatayu \{\}
>> scene forest clear
>> enter jatayu from left to 0.5 in 0.1
>> set jatayu pose=grieve y=0
>> music grief
He lies where he fell, with his wings beside him, still breathing. Above him the Pushpaka turns south.
-> END
